# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LOCAL CONFIG OVERRIDES — example / template
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to config.local.yaml (gitignored — never committed)
# and fill in your real values. load_config() (src/config.py) deep-
# merges this on top of config.yaml at runtime: any key you set here
# replaces the same key in config.yaml, nothing else changes.
#
# This exists for settings that aren't secrets (they don't need to be
# a GitHub Secret / env var) but ARE personally identifying — the
# clearest example is which Craigslist metro regions to search, since
# that reveals your approximate location. Keeping this file gitignored
# means config.yaml can stay committed (and this repo can stay public)
# without exposing where you live.
#
# In CI (GitHub Actions), this file doesn't exist on the runner by
# default — .github/workflows/scrape.yml and scrape-staging.yml write
# it themselves from the CRAIGSLIST_REGIONS_YAML GitHub Secret before
# the scraper runs, so production/staging still search your real
# regions without them ever touching the repo.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Example only — replace with the real metro regions you want to
# search. Region slugs are the last path segment of a Craigslist
# metro's URL, e.g. https://newyork.craigslist.org -> "newyork".
# List as many as you want; the scraper aggregates results across
# all of them (see sites.craigslist's comments in config.yaml).
sites:
  craigslist:
    regions:
      - "newyork"
      - "chicago"
      - "houston"
